nemeton — Third-Party Data Attributions
========================================

This NOTICE lists the third-party datasets and models that the
`nemeton` R package may consume at runtime via its data-source
abstraction (ADR-002). Including the ability to consume a dataset
does not imply that the dataset itself is bundled with the package;
for the most part, only configuration, schemas, and derived
statistics are stored here.

IGN BD ORTHO®
-------------
Source   : Institut national de l'information géographique et forestière
           (IGN), https://geoservices.ign.fr/bdortho
License  : Licence Ouverte / Open Licence version 2.0 (Etalab 2.0)
Usage    : Base imagery for the opencanopy Canopy Height Model
           (CHM) workflow (see spec 005 phase 1).

Open-Canopy pre-trained weights and benchmark dataset
-----------------------------------------------------
Reference: Fogel, F., Perret, M., Cafferata, S., Chassaing, M.,
           Lobry, S., Landrieu, L. (2024). "Open-Canopy: A Country-
           Scale Benchmark for Canopy Height Estimation at Very High
           Resolution."
Source   : https://huggingface.co/datasets/AI4Forest/Open-Canopy
           https://github.com/fajwel/Open-Canopy
License  : MIT (code) / CC-BY-4.0 (data) — to be confirmed at commit
           for the specific release consumed.
Usage    : Pre-trained UNet / PVTv2 weights and benchmark data used
           by the downstream `opencanopy` R package
           (pobsteta/opencanopynemeton) to produce CHM rasters fed
           into `nemeton::sanitize_chm()`.

Derived CHM (opencanopy artefact)
---------------------------------
The Canopy Height Model raster produced by the `opencanopy` package
is a DERIVATIVE WORK of the two sources above. Any redistribution of
a derived CHM must carry a double attribution:
  - IGN BD ORTHO® — Licence Ouverte / Etalab 2.0,
  - Fogel et al. 2024 — Open-Canopy (license of the specific release).

